  "database": "rschema_0344",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0344 database is designed to manage and track various aspects of web services and their interactions with users. At its core, the database contains information about users, which are identified by a unique user ID and can be associated with a username and email address. Each user can have multiple permissions, which are tied to specific applications, and these permissions are stored in the Permissions table, which also links users to the applications they have access to. The Applications table contains details about the applications themselves, including a unique application ID, code, name, and type. The Web_Service table stores information about the web services offered by these applications, including the application they belong to, a unique service ID, creation date, description, and name. The Error_Information table tracks any errors that occur during service interactions, including the service ID, error code, error description, occurrence time, and return status. The Service_Monitoring table logs the monitoring data for these services, including the call time, delay time, return status, and service ID. The Statistics table provides statistics about the services, including the call count, service ID, success rate, and time period. The Error_and_Monitoring_Association table links error information to service monitoring data, allowing for a comprehensive view of service interactions and errors.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis system is designed for managing and monitoring web services in various applications. Key requirements include:\nEach user has a unique username, email, and role. User roles are associated with specific permissions. Users can be assigned different roles and permissions that are linked to particular applications.\nEach application has a unique ID, code, name, and type.\nEach web service has a unique ID, name, description, and creation date. It records error information, including error codes, descriptions, timestamps, and return status.\nMonitors the invocation of web services, recording details like invocation time, return status, delay time, and other performance metrics.\nTracks statistics such as success rate and call count over a specific time period.\nTracks which users are authorized to access which applications.\nLinks error data with monitoring data to enable detailed analysis and reporting.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0344.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0344\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `applications` (\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`application_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`permission_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `permissions_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `permissions_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`application_id`) REFERENCES `applications` (`application_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `web_services` (\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `application_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`service_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `web_services_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`application_id`) REFERENCES `applications` (`application_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `error_information` (\n  `error_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `error_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `error_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `occurrence_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `return_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`error_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `error_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `web_services` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_monitoring` (\n  `monitoring_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `call_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `delay_time` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `return_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`monitoring_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `service_monitoring_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `web_services` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `statistics` (\n  `statistic_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `call_count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `success_rate` float NOT NULL,\n  `time_period` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`statistic_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `statistics_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `web_services` (`service_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `error_and_monitoring_association` (\n  `association_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `error_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `monitoring_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`association_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `error_and_monitoring_association_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`error_id`) REFERENCES `error_information` (`error_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `error_and_monitoring_association_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`monitoring_id`) REFERENCES `service_monitoring` (`monitoring_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
